1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,180
InsightIQ is now Lead Trace.

2
00:00:02,340 --> 00:00:07,984
We listened to feedback from industry professionals and used it to shape a broader
direction for our project.

3
00:00:08,145 --> 00:00:13,729
Today, Lead Trace brings prospect research, source evidence, and deal briefs
together.

4
00:00:13,889 --> 00:00:20,033
We are building toward lead generation, customer relationship management, and
connected sales workflows.

5
00:00:20,193 --> 00:00:23,744
Those features are planned, and we will refine them as we progress.

6
00:00:23,904 --> 00:00:26,657
Start with a prospect and describe what you sell.

7
00:00:26,817 --> 00:00:29,869
Choose meeting preparation or personalized outreach.

8
00:00:30,029 --> 00:00:33,998
The application keeps your prospect, offer, and goal together.

9
00:00:34,158 --> 00:00:36,104
Research runs in the background.

10
00:00:36,264 --> 00:00:42,673
The system finds public sources, extracts relevant claims, and builds a brief with
the evidence attached.

11
00:00:42,833 --> 00:00:47,324
Each conversation angle connects a source claim to a possible fit for your offer.

12
00:00:47,484 --> 00:00:50,197
A question helps you test whether that fit is real.

13
00:00:50,357 --> 00:00:52,885
Hypotheses stay separate from facts.

14
00:00:53,045 --> 00:00:57,078
Open a source, check the gaps, and review the outreach draft.

15
00:00:57,238 --> 00:01:01,116
Copy a question or download the complete brief for your own workflow.

16
00:01:01,276 --> 00:01:03,538
These screens use demonstration data.

17
00:01:03,698 --> 00:01:08,629
Our next stage expands that research foundation toward lead generation and CRM.

18
00:01:08,789 --> 00:01:11,947
The feature set and release plans are still taking shape.

19
